      "scenario": {
        "id": "lpic1-editor-handover",
        "version": 1,
        "track": "LPIC-1",
        "unit": "standard-editor-handover",
        "topic": "Default editor and saved-file handover",
        "title": "Configure an inherited editor and complete a handover",
        "summary": "Repair the editor setting across sample environments, then use its actual inherited choice to maintain a virtual handover file.",
        "objective": "Configure inherited EDITOR from each supplied PREFERRED_EDITOR without changing TEAM or printing setup output. Open the handover file with that choice, replace OWNER legacy with exactly one OWNER platform record and add exactly one REVIEW ready record. Preserve all other complete lines and the operator note, save the file and check the handover.",
        "difficulty": "Intermediate",
        "minutes": 20,
        "steps": [
          "Understand the task, run the setup against its sample environments, open the simulated editor, repair the handover and check saved outcomes."
        ],
        "guide": [],
        "explanation": "An exported EDITOR reaches the application's child environment; an ordinary private value does not. The samples with no existing export catch a setup that only happens to work when EDITOR was inherited. The application reads its actual inherited choice, then the saved handover must contain the required records without losing other lines. Editing the buffer alone is not enough: write it before checking.",
        "hints": [
          "PREFERRED_EDITOR and TEAM are supplied by each sample. EDITOR is the setting your setup creates or replaces; a fixed choice will not satisfy every sample.",
          "A value can be correct in the setup but missing in the child. Inspect each actual result and the export attribute rather than printing a look-alike report.",
          "After opening the handover, search for the complete OWNER record before removing it. Add the requested records while preserving the ticket and safety note, then :w and Enter."
        ],
        "sources": [
          "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-101-102-objectives/#103.8",
          "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/bash.1.html#ENVIRONMENT",
          "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/crontab.1.html",
          "https://vimhelp.org/intro.txt.html",
          "https://vimhelp.org/editing.txt.html",
          "https://nano-editor.org/dist/latest/nano.html"
        ],
        "simplifications": "Existing bounded in-process shell and vi-style editor, not a host shell or editor. The simulated handover application consults EDITOR only and accepts the exact supplied names vi and vim; other programs can use VISUAL or different defaults. No flags, editor paths, host programs or profile edits. Nano/Emacs are supporting awareness only, not emulated editors. Setup samples have separate environments; the supplied handover virtual files are edited separately. Full vi syntax and other LPIC objectives remain outside this activity.",
        "prerequisites": []
      },
